@startuml architecture-components
!theme plain
title Tender Watch — Component Architecture (agent ↔ RAG ↔ memory ↔ external APIs)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

actor "Timer /\nPOST /run-now" as Trigger
actor "Slack user\n(clicks Bid / No-Bid)" as SlackUser

package "loop-orchestrator (the Agent)" {
  component "LoopRunner\n(Discover → Assess →\nProcurementMethodPolicy filter →\nPersist → Handoff)" as Runner
  component "IMcpTenderClient\n(McpTenderClient)" as McpClient
  component "AnthropicClient\n(agentic tool-use loop +\nstructured JSON output)" as Anthropic
  component "SlackNotifier\n(outgoing: Block Kit blocks\nwith interactive buttons)" as Slack
  component "SlackInteractionHandler\n(POST /slack/interactions —\nHMAC signature verification)" as SlackInteraction
  component "DecisionUpdater\n(pure: applies Bid/NoBid)" as DecisionUpdater
  component "ITenderStateStore\n(TableStorageStateStore)" as StateStore

  package "RAG" {
    component "IEligibilityIndex\n(InMemoryEligibilityIndex)" as Index
    component "MarkdownChunker" as Chunker
    component "IEmbeddingClient\n(OpenAiEmbeddingClient)" as Embedder
  }
}

package "mcp-server" {
  component "MCP tools\n(list_tenders, search_tenders,\nget_tender — incl. tenderId /\nprocurementMethod / items[],\nget_company_profile)" as McpTools
  component "CompanyProfileService" as ProfileSvc
}

package "Memory" {
  database "Azure Table Storage\n\"TenderReview\" table\n(Azurite locally)\npartitions: run-state |\ntender reviews | prompt proposals" as Table
}

package "External APIs" {
  cloud "Prozorro public\nprocurement API" as Prozorro
  cloud "Anthropic Messages API\n(claude-haiku-4-5,\nstructured outputs)" as AnthropicApi
  cloud "OpenAI Embeddings API\n(text-embedding-3-small)" as OpenAiApi
  cloud "Slack\n(incoming webhook +\nInteractivity & Shortcuts)" as SlackApi
}

file "data/qualification-docs/*.md" as QualDocs
file "data/company-profile.json" as ProfileFile

Trigger --> Runner : triggers one pass

Runner --> McpClient : Discover (list_tenders) /\nAssess's deterministic\nget_tender pre-fetch
McpClient --> McpTools : MCP Streamable HTTP\n(X-Api-Key)
McpTools --> Prozorro : HTTPS
McpTools --> ProfileSvc
ProfileSvc --> ProfileFile : reads at request time

Runner --> Index : Assess\n(query eligibility snippets)
Index --> Chunker : chunk at startup
Chunker --> QualDocs : reads once
Index --> Embedder : embed chunks + query
Embedder --> OpenAiApi : HTTPS

Runner --> Anthropic : Assess (agentic + structured) /\nHandoff (structured)
Anthropic --> AnthropicApi : HTTPS
Anthropic ..> McpClient : during Assess: tool_use(get_tender/\nsearch_tenders) routed back through\nAssessStage's own executor — genuinely\nLLM-decided MCP calls, allow-listed in code\n(not Claude calling mcp-server directly —\nAnthropic's API returns a tool_use block,\nAssessStage executes it against McpClient)

Runner --> StateStore : Persist +\nseen-tender-ID idempotency guard
StateStore --> Table : Azure.Data.Tables SDK

Runner --> Slack : Handoff\n(uncertain / high-value eligible,\nnot procurementMethod=limited)
Slack --> SlackApi : HTTPS POST\n{text, blocks}

SlackUser --> SlackApi : clicks a button
SlackApi --> SlackInteraction : POST /slack/interactions\n(signed block_actions payload)
SlackInteraction --> DecisionUpdater : ApplyDecision(existing, bid/nobid)
SlackInteraction --> StateStore : UpsertAsync(HumanDecision)
SlackInteraction --> SlackApi : POST response_url\n(hide buttons, Ukrainian\nconfirmation line — best-effort)

note right of Runner
  Every stage + every LLM call is
  wrapped in its own OpenTelemetry
  Activity (TenderWatch.LoopOrchestrator.Stages),
  exported to the Aspire Dashboard /
  Azure Monitor as one connected trace
  per run — nested MCP tool spans
  come along for free via W3C
  trace-context propagation over HTTP.
end note

note right of SlackInteraction
  Fails closed (503) if SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET
  is unset — never accepts an unverified
  request. Signature = HMAC-SHA256 of
  "v0:{timestamp}:{rawBody}", rejects
  requests older than 5 minutes.
end note

note bottom of StateStore
  The self-improvement ("hill-climbing")
  outer loop — AnalysisBackgroundWorker,
  AnalysisRunner, PromptGuardrails — reads
  from and writes to this same store,
  and reuses AnthropicClient / SlackNotifier
  above. Kept out of this diagram for
  readability — see
  architecture-analysis.puml.
end note

@enduml
